# Fault scen_ask_world (writer 6): `ask q: x.cash.amount for x in transfers over 2025-01-01..2025-12-31 in sc` in a
# scenario file was refused LOAD-WORLD: the span's end read `in sc` as a membership test. L §2.3 parse rule 4: "On an ask
# line, in ID after the body and its for names the world". L §6.4 (round 11b): amt and gday are inputs the scenario
# declares, so their rows may govern always. gift moves 7.00 DUK into konto (opening 5.00) on 2025-03-01: q = 7.00 DUK,
# r = 12.00 DUK. Writer 7: q's line now lists the instance it binds, unfulfilled: gift (L §8.2; writer 6's known gap,
# L8_2_for_unfulfilled_per_line.test).
=== b.tally
model b
  tally 2
  on 2025-12-31
  start 2025-01-01
  end 2025-12-31

source s "s"

source t "t"

unit DUK: currency minor 0.01

place konto: accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..
=== sc.tally
scenario sc over b
  tally 2
  from 2025-01-01

place world: outside lives 2025-01-01..

input amt: money DUK

input gday: date

move gift: transfers
  on gday
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt

ask q: x.cash.amount for x in transfers over 2025-01-01..2025-12-31 in sc

ask r: bal(konto, 2025-12-31) in sc

version v
  cite t
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  amt = 7.00 "a"
  gday = 2025-03-01 "g"
  opening[konto] = 5.00 at 2025-01-01 start "o"
=== expect
q (x = gift): 7.00 DUK
  world: sc
  unfulfilled: gift
  cut 2025-12-31
r: 12.00 DUK
  world: sc
  unfulfilled: gift
  cut 2025-12-31
